From 42bd3da245c889d5c2945828fb31ef694f79d7e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Henault <contact@adamhlt.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:04:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: add per-process HPC filtering

Add a kernel/hpc subsystem that gates RISC-V hardware performance
counters on context switch and trap entry so that only the events of a
selected PID are accounted.

- entry.S: stop/restart counters on U-mode trap entry/exit
- sched/core.c: account/switch counters on context switch
- new syscalls 441-450 (hpc_config, hpc_read, hpc_reset, hpc_start,
  hpc_stop, hpc_toggle_debug, hpc_toggle_filtering, hpc_set_pid_filter)
- SBI interface to the matching OpenSBI vendor extension
- debugfs log of filtered samples
---
